  "details": "Right now when you select a user and look at the options for avatar there are three options.\n\n1. Force on\n\n2. Don't show (make them a robot)\n\n3. Use security settings\n\nI never use the second, but maybe someone does. \n\nWhat I'd like to see if an option to kinda opt in to showing an avatar, but with a way I can apply some sort of limit to it. For the purposes of having a sensible feature request, I would like to opt in to bypassing shield options, but I'd like to hide avatars that I find use too many effects, if a user is using an annoying avatar, I'd rather see the fallback.\n\nWith the current system I have it's best to have conservative settings for avatars and then if I actually interact with someone I can make sure I see the avatar. But it's annoying if they change from something reasonable into an avatar with a million polygons. \n\nIf I could half way show avatar for them I could tell VRChat to never show me the 1 million polygon lag fest. For now I turn thier avatar off and then maybe check back later to see if they change out.",
